// Workspace: the floor and the layer above it resolve each other locally, so a change
// to core/go is visible to sdk/go without a push and a pseudo-version bump. Consumers
// never see this file — they resolve sdk/go's require line from GitHub.
go 1.25

use (
	./cli/go
	./server/go
	./core/go
	./sdk/go
)

// `use` above already points at these directories, and for a build made only of workspace
// modules that is enough. The moment a member gains a dependency from OUTSIDE the
// workspace — custody brought cli/go its first (ADR 0007 §A) — the module graph is
// computed the ordinary way, and the require lines below are looked up as real versions.
// Bitspark/archon is private, so a CI runner has no credentials for that lookup and the
// build dies on `git ls-remote` while a developer machine sails through on GOPRIVATE plus
// a token. These replaces say what `use` already means, unconditionally.
replace github.com/Bitspark/archon/core/go v0.6.1 => ./core/go

replace github.com/Bitspark/archon/sdk/go v0.6.1 => ./sdk/go
